// 5.63: a coupled element may declare a yield stress -- it belongs to the 3D
// partner region's fluid, not to a wall on this row. The detailed region still
// reports the whole drop of that region, and the transient row charges only
// R*q: no static branch is inserted here, so the wall is never billed twice.
// The checker asserts that the transient trace is bit-identical to a twin case
// with the three rheology keys removed. This used to be the third member of the
// refusal family (steady 5.46 / transient 5.48); both refusals are now lifted.
// The name keeps `reject` only for historical continuity.
// verified by tests/check_transient_yield_static_hold.py (family 6).
fluid { rho 850; mu 0.1; }
nodes { A { fixedPressure 3.0e4; } B { fixedPressure 2.0e4; } }
pipes { Bad { from A; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02;
              coupledResistance 5.0e8; yieldStress 1.0; } }
time  { dt 0.02; endTime 0.1; reportEvery 1; }
